            <ArticleTitle>Sympathetically maintained pain of the digits in porphyria cutanea tarda relieved by i.v. regional guanethidine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>79-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a sympathetically maintained pain of the tips of the fingers in a 39-year-old man with porphyria cutanea tarda is presented. Occupational vibrating trauma is the presumed cause. The successful treatment with intravenous regional guanethidine is reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
